# Product UI

- Read `docs/PRODUCT.md`, `docs/SCOPE.md`, `docs/FEATURE_STATUS.md`, and `docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md` before changing user-facing UI.
- Use **KorKru / ก่อครู** and the adaptable line **“ก่อ…โดยครู”**; do not lock “ก่อการเรียนรู้ โดยครู” as the permanent slogan.
- Write user-facing copy in clear Thai. Keep code identifiers and standard technical terms in English.
- Do not present mock analytics, invoices, usage, pricing, compliance, security, or unfinished actions as real.
- State clearly which answers are auto-graded and which require teacher review.
- Keep forms keyboard-accessible with visible labels, useful errors, and pending states.
- Respect responsive layouts, color contrast, and `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Use existing UI primitives and visual tokens before introducing one-off patterns.
